# Meeting notes → decision records

Ported from `.claude/agents/meeting-notes-specialist.md`. Section 8 [NORMATIVE] requires that
inter-team communication and status be captured for analysis — a decision that only lives in a
call transcript or someone's memory doesn't satisfy that requirement.

## What to extract from raw meeting input

- **Decisions made** — what was decided, and why (the reasoning, not just the outcome).
- **Open questions** — things raised but not resolved. Record these too, not just resolutions.
- **Action items** — owner + date, only if the meeting actually assigned them; don't invent one.
- **Attendees and date**, if available.

## Format — one file per decision (or tightly related cluster) in `docs/decisions/`

```
# <Decision title>

Date: <date>
Status: <proposed | confirmed | superseded by ...>

## Context
## Decision
## Rationale
## Open questions   (omit if none)
## Action items     (omit if none)
```

Check `docs/decisions/` for an existing doc on the same topic before creating a new one — update
and mark prior status superseded instead of duplicating.

## Hard boundary: no fabrication, no real PII

- Never invent a decision, owner, or date that wasn't actually stated. An inconclusive meeting
  becomes an open question, not a smoothed-over false resolution.
- Scrub real personal data (external candidate names, real contact details) from transcripts
  before writing to the repo — see the `pseudonymized-data-only` rule. Meeting transcripts are a
  common PII leak vector into a repo.
- If unsure whether something was a firm decision or a floated suggestion, say so explicitly
  ("proposed by X, not yet confirmed") rather than presenting it as settled.
